ependent polling showing her ahead could shift this toward Tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Nancy Mace (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Nancy Mace's retirement leaves this Charleston-area seat open, and Republicans nominated Jenny Costa Honeycutt while Democrats tapped Nancy Lacore, a former Navy official. The district leans Republican by about six points, and most expert raters call the race Likely or Lean R, though a few see it as closer. Prediction markets give Honeycutt roughly a two-in-three edge.\n\nLacore has outraised Honeycutt by a wide margin and earned DCCC Red to Blue support, and the only recent polls, both Democratic-sponsored, show a single-digit race. The forecast lands on a modest Republican advantage with meaningful uncertainty, since polling here is sparse and the open-seat dynamic invites volatility.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.2812, "margin": -3.39}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2869, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.2863, "margin": -4.0}]}